// -- The engines -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

// The engines, as Mandel's profile and plan draw them and the studio's 44-inch model has them (photographs on the
// Catacombs site, cited, not reproduced): four, in a diamond seen from astern.  Each is a bell, a collar at its
// throat, a neck through a flange ring to a tank behind it -- a pill, a cylinder 0.55 round with rounded ends, from
// 9.5 to 7.75 aft of the middle -- and its bell is a shell, ringed once near its mouth and five times a third of the
// way up, closed inside at its throat by a plate with five small nozzles in it, four round one, as the SpaceCraft
// sheet's stern view draws them.  The bell's outside is the plan's, measured: 0.735 round at the mouth, 0.42 at the
// throat, 1.33 along.

// The bell, its collar and its neck, about the bell's axis along +Y from its mouth: radius, distance from the mouth.
