// The laboratory pod: the passenger module's body without its windows and side doors, and across its middle a block
// standing out to either side, as the studio's model has it (Starship Modeler's photographs, cited, not
// reproduced).  The block is 3.0 along the craft where it meets the body and tapers to 1.5 at its outer faces, 1.7
// out from the body's sides; seen from an end it is an octagon, its outer faces upright from 1.53 to 3.18, a broad
// chamfer above, ribbed, and a narrow one below.  In each outer face, the end door, drawn down to fit; in each
// slanted face, a dark square recess crossed by an X, a cluster of thrusters in it; under each side, a foot.  Its
// top stands a hair above the body's and its underside a hair below the well in the body's, so no face of the
// one lies in a face of the other.
EagleLaboratoryBody = group {
    difference {
        extrusion {
            path {
                move to -1.2700, -2.2750
                line to -1.2700, 2.2750
